    "body": "The previous cue-only fit produced finite gradients but changed no packed native coefficient. This adds a matched intervention at the consistently driven lane1/bin3 coefficient123: baseline -0.25, credit-preferred -0.5, and opposite-control 0.0. All other cue coefficients and prefix/Period/Stop payloads stay frozen, with independently reloaded and honestly rebound native chains.\n\nThe probe verifies the actual consumed-address Q24 change, retains full development canonical and own-prefix traces, reports source margins and paired source/generation gains and losses, and selects by baseline-inclusive development token loss before exposed diagnostic predictions. There is no optimizer, new runtime floating-point path, or transformer. It updates the current roadmap with the measured quantization barrier and conditional next decisions.\n\nValidation at numerical head002c9a75a6ea76dd6348ae17067ce87787832082: independent source review PASS; 1,296 tracked build-source hashes verified; all30 bank-fit tests plus1 sibling rejection PASS; rustfmt and release build PASS on the existing Linux pod, CPU16/CUDA hidden. Checks68.185s, peak2.715GB. Final34764445 changes only result/plan documentation; claims/diff gates PASS, Rust bytes unchanged, no final-head compile claimed.\n\nActual native probe completes: preferred CE0.962570925 versus baseline0.966180663; opposite0.976521601. Preferred source80→81/128, paired24→25/64, first token70→71/128; opposite79/23/69. Complete replies23/128 and exposed diagnostic15/32 source,1/32 complete remain unchanged. Actual consumed-address score changes verified in10 rows. Worker20.030s, peak1.698GB. Independent receipt review supports a small directional result only. Next is bounded native discrete-update calibration with row/pair harm tracking; no general attention/chat/transfer claim. Durable evidence is under /workspace/uor-r4/codex/geometric-cue-calibration-20261005/quantum-1.\n\nThis stacked draft and its parents are unmerged.\n\nReferences #1552, #820.\n",
